\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {41}{\ignorespaces  Total interaction cross section for the system $^{12}$C + $^{12}$C as a function of beam energy. The blue, green, and red circles represent the reaction cross section measurements obtained in the present work using carbon targets of thickness 5.4~mm, 10.86~mm, and 21.98~mm, respectively. The corresponding charge-changing cross sections are shown as semi-transparent stars in the same color coding. Light green symbols denote previous data from L. Ponnath et al.~\cite  {ponnath2023precise} for the same target configurations. Purple squares indicate earlier experimental results from the literature: 370~AMeV (Takechi et al.~\cite  {takechi2009reaction}), 790~AMeV (Tanihata et al.~\cite  {tanihata1990rnbeams}), and 950~AMeV (Ozawa et al.~\cite  {ozawa2001measurements}). For comparison, black circles show theoretical predictions based on Glauber model calculations, while red diamonds indicate Glauber calculations including in-medium modifications such as Coulomb and Pauli blocking effects, as discussed in Section~\ref  {sec:glauber_ext}.  \relax }}{93}{figure.caption.46}}
\newlabel{fig:tot_interaction_cs}{{41}{93}{Total interaction cross section for the system $^{12}$C + $^{12}$C as a function of beam energy. The blue, green, and red circles represent the reaction cross section measurements obtained in the present work using carbon targets of thickness 5.4~mm, 10.86~mm, and 21.98~mm, respectively. The corresponding charge-changing cross sections are shown as semi-transparent stars in the same color coding. Light green symbols denote previous data from L. Ponnath et al.~\cite {ponnath2023precise} for the same target configurations. Purple squares indicate earlier experimental results from the literature: 370~AMeV (Takechi et al.~\cite {takechi2009reaction}), 790~AMeV (Tanihata et al.~\cite {tanihata1990rnbeams}), and 950~AMeV (Ozawa et al.~\cite {ozawa2001measurements}). For comparison, black circles show theoretical predictions based on Glauber model calculations, while red diamonds indicate Glauber calculations including in-medium modifications such as Coulomb and Pauli blocking effects, as discussed in Section~\ref {sec:glauber_ext}.  \relax }{figure.caption.46}{}}
\newlabel{fig:tot_interaction_cs@cref}{{[figure][41][]41}{[1][92][]93}}
\newlabel{fig:final_res_cc_ti}{{41}{93}{Total interaction cross section for the system $^{12}$C + $^{12}$C as a function of beam energy. The blue, green, and red circles represent the reaction cross section measurements obtained in the present work using carbon targets of thickness 5.4~mm, 10.86~mm, and 21.98~mm, respectively. The corresponding charge-changing cross sections are shown as semi-transparent stars in the same color coding. Light green symbols denote previous data from L. Ponnath et al.~\cite {ponnath2023precise} for the same target configurations. Purple squares indicate earlier experimental results from the literature: 370~AMeV (Takechi et al.~\cite {takechi2009reaction}), 790~AMeV (Tanihata et al.~\cite {tanihata1990rnbeams}), and 950~AMeV (Ozawa et al.~\cite {ozawa2001measurements}). For comparison, black circles show theoretical predictions based on Glauber model calculations, while red diamonds indicate Glauber calculations including in-medium modifications such as Coulomb and Pauli blocking effects, as discussed in Section~\ref {sec:glauber_ext}.  \relax }{figure.caption.46}{}}
