\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {52}{\ignorespaces  Doppler-corrected $\gamma $-ray spectrum in coincidence with the $^{12}\mathrm  {C}(p,2p)^{11}\mathrm  {B}$ quasi-free scattering reaction in the 2~cm CH$_2$ target. The prominent peak at $E_{\gamma } \approx 2.1\tmspace  +\thinmuskip {.1667em}\mathrm  {MeV}$ corresponds to the de-excitation of the $^{11}\mathrm  {B}$ nucleus from its first excited state ($1/2^-$) to the ground state. This peak is fitted with a Gaussian function (blue), while the underlying background is described by an exponential distribution (green). A broader and less well-defined structure is observed at $E_{\gamma } \approx 5\tmspace  +\thinmuskip {.1667em}\mathrm  {MeV}$, associated with the de-excitation of the $3/2^-$ state and its corresponding single escape peak. Due to the still rather incomplete geometry of CALIFA this high energy signal is slightly shifted to lower energies due to loss of energy by Bremsstrahlung. \relax }}{117}{figure.caption.59}}
\newlabel{fig:gamma_spec_12c_p2p_11b}{{52}{117}{Doppler-corrected $\gamma $-ray spectrum in coincidence with the $^{12}\mathrm {C}(p,2p)^{11}\mathrm {B}$ quasi-free scattering reaction in the 2~cm CH$_2$ target. The prominent peak at $E_{\gamma } \approx 2.1\,\mathrm {MeV}$ corresponds to the de-excitation of the $^{11}\mathrm {B}$ nucleus from its first excited state ($1/2^-$) to the ground state. This peak is fitted with a Gaussian function (blue), while the underlying background is described by an exponential distribution (green). A broader and less well-defined structure is observed at $E_{\gamma } \approx 5\,\mathrm {MeV}$, associated with the de-excitation of the $3/2^-$ state and its corresponding single escape peak. Due to the still rather incomplete geometry of CALIFA this high energy signal is slightly shifted to lower energies due to loss of energy by Bremsstrahlung. \relax }{figure.caption.59}{}}
\newlabel{fig:gamma_spec_12c_p2p_11b@cref}{{[figure][52][]52}{[1][116][]117}}
